ubstantial","introduced_date":"2025-02-12","is_demo":false,"label":"S. 545","latest_action":{"date":"2026-04-15","text":"Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 372."},"policy_area":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsor":{"chamber":"Senate","district":null,"id":"C001113","name":"Sen. Cortez Masto, Catherine","party":"D","state":"NV"},"stage":"on_calendar","stage_label":"On a chamber calendar","summary":"The Combating Illicit Xylazine Act regulates xylazine—an animal sedative and pain reliever—by placing it under schedule III of the Controlled Substances Act. This change creates criminal penalties for manufacturing, distributing, dispensing, or possessing xylazine for illicit use, while establishing exemptions for lawful animal care, veterinary uses, and government wildlife or animal-control programs.","summary_threshold":50,"title":"Combating Illicit Xylazine Act","viability":64.5,"viability_status":"active"},"date":"2026-04-15","detail":"Related bill","id":"119-s-545","label":"S. 545","title":"Combating Illicit Xylazine Act","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/545"}]},"selection":{"reason":"Impact scored and summarised by Gemini.","status":"analyzed"},"sources":{"latest":{"date":"2026-09-16","label":"Placed on Calendar Senate","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1266/BILLS-119hr1266pcs.htm"},"other":[{"label":"This bill on Congress.gov","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1266"}],"past":[{"date":"2026-09-15","label":"Engrossed in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1266/BILLS-119hr1266eh.htm"},{"date":"2026-09-14","label":"Reported in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1266/BILLS-119hr1266rh.htm"},{"date":"2025-02-12","label":"Introduced in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1266/BILLS-119hr1266ih.htm"}]},"sponsor":{"chamber":"House","district":"19","id":"P000613","name":"Rep. Panetta, Jimmy","party":"D","state":"CA"},"stage":"passed_origin","stage_label":"Passed one chamber","summary":"H.R. 1266, the Combating Illicit Xylazine Act, adds xylazine to Schedule III of the Controlled Substances Act. Xylazine is a nonopioid sedative and pain reliever approved for animal use. The bill establishes criminal penalties for illicit manufacturing, distribution, and dispensing, provides specific exemptions for legitimate animal and wildlife uses, requires tracking in the DEA drug reporting system, and directs federal agencies to report on illicit use and trafficking.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"They are exempt from physical security capital expenditure requirements and receive expedited processing for relevant manufacturer submissions, with labeling and distribution logistics requirements taking effect one year after enactment.","group":"Manufacturers of xylazine"},{"effect":"They must comply with practitioner registration, inventory, and recordkeeping requirements within 60 days unless an application is pending, and they may lawfully dispense xylazine.","group":"Veterinarians and pharmacies"},{"effect":"Individuals or businesses possessing xylazine lawfully obtained for animals, government animal-control programs, or wildlife programs do not need to register under the Controlled Substances Act.","group":"Ultimate users possessing xylazine for animals"},{"effect":"They are subject to criminal penalties under the Controlled Substances Act, and the U.S. Sentencing Commission is directed to review and amend sentencing guidelines.","group":"Individuals involved in illicit xylazine offenses"}],"key_provisions":["Adds xylazine, including its salts, isomers, and salts of isomers, to schedule III of the Controlled Substances Act.","Subjects illicit manufacturing, distributing, dispensing, or possession with intent to manufacture, distribute, or dispense xylazine to criminal penalties.","Exempts certain persons and entities possessing xylazine lawfully dispensed by a veterinarian or pharmacy for animals, animal-control, or wildlife programs from DEA registration.","Exempts xylazine manufacturers from physical security capital expenditure requirements under schedule III.","Requires xylazine transactions to be tracked in the drug reporting system maintained by the DEA.","Directs the DEA and the Food and Drug Administration to report to Congress on the prevalence and impact of illicit xylazine use, trafficking, and misuse."],"missing_information":["Specific details on the exact length of criminal prison sentences or exact monetary fine amounts under the new penalties.","Exact budgetary costs or appropriations required to implement the reporting, tracking, and agency coordination."],"plain_summary":"H.R. 1266, the Combating Illicit Xylazine Act, adds xylazine to Schedule III of the Controlled Substances Act. Xylazine is a nonopioid sedative and pain reliever approved for animal use. The bill establishes criminal penalties for illicit manufacturing, distribution, and dispensing, provides specific exemptions for legitimate animal and wildlife uses, requires tracking in the DEA drug reporting system, and directs federal agencies to report on illicit use and trafficking.","significance":"The bill places a nationally regulated animal sedative used in illicit drug mixtures under Schedule III federal control, enacting tracking, reporting, and criminal penalties while carving out specific regulatory exemptions and transitions for legitimate animal care and manufacturing entities."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T21:05:51+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1266/BILLS-119hr1266pcs.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Combating Illicit Xylazine Act","viability":85.3,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"Passed one chamber"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"Stage val